  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "szf2LeMmKTpSpGUKk2Jrri/DdnQ=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:29:51.533Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "`docs/specs/migrate-codegen-fixes.md` is a punch list from migrating `packages/vetra` with `ph-cli migrate` + `ph-cli generate`, and its three goals set the bar: a second migration on a similar legacy project should produce a tree that **builds without manual intervention**, `ph-cli generate processor --all` should be **safe to re-run** on a tree with hand-written processor files, and the migrated `tsconfig.json` should compile without TS6305.\n\nTwo defects are worth carrying as warnings for anyone running the tooling today:\n\n**`--dir <path>` scaffolds a directory named after the absolute path.** `cmd-ts`'s `Directory` type resolves to an absolute path and the code calls `dirname(...)`, returning its *parent*, which is then joined onto `processors/`. The result is a directory like `processors/users-acaldas-dev-powerhouse-monorepo-packages-vetra-processors/` and a matching identifier in `switchboard.ts` (`clis/ph-cli/src/services/generate-processor.ts:41-44`). The fix is `basename(dir)`, or computing the name relative to the project's `processors/` directory and rejecting paths outside it.\n\n**`updateFactoryBuildersFile` always runs, even when `factory.ts` is preserved.** `makeIndexFile` / `makeProcessorFile` / `makeFactoryFile` correctly bail out with `if (alreadyExists) return;`, but the factory-builders updater appends `import { <camel>FactoryBuilder } from \"processors/<kebab>\";` and pushes the symbol regardless. If the preserved `factory.ts` exports a different name \u2014 a legacy `<camel>ProcessorFactory`, say \u2014 the generated `switchboard.ts` / `connect.ts` **will not compile**.\n\n## Provenance\n- `docs/specs/migrate-codegen-fixes.md` \u2014 Goals; Issues 1 and 2\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:29:51.533Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:29:51.533Z"
    }
  },
